                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ReferencesDoubledSupergeometry"} Doubled super-geometry
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %em Type II geometry
            (often
            %em doubled geometry
            as in “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+field+theory"}> double field theory
            ”) is to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+geometry"} Riemannian geometry
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+complex+geometry"} generalized complex geometry
            is to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+geometry"} complex geometry
          %p
            Where the latter is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
            induced by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduction+of+the+structure+group"} reduction of the structure group
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+tangent+bundle"} generalized tangent bundle
            of an even dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            along the inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 2
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(d,d) \to O(2d,2d)
            of the indefinite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+group"} unitary group
            into the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+group"} orthogonal group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+group"} orthogonal groups
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  O(n) \times O(n) \to O(n,n)
                  \\,,
          %p
            which is the inclusion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+compact+subgroup"} maximal compact subgroup
            into the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Narain+group"} Narain group
          %p
            This notion takes its name from the fact that it describes a good bit of the geometry of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+supergravity"} type II supergravity
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            The definition of type II geometry proceeds in direct analogy with that of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+geometry"} Riemannian geometry
            in terms of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+structure"} orthogonal structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vielbein"} vielbein
            fields on the tangent bundle, generalized here to the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+tangent+bundle"} generalized tangent bundle
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#FiberwiseMetric"} As a fiberwise metric on the generalized tangent bundle
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#ReductionOfStructureGroup"} By reduction of the structure group of the generalized tangent bundle
          %h3#FiberwiseMetric By fiberwise metric on the generalized tangent bundle
          %p (…)
          %h3#ReductionOfStructureGroup By reduction of the generalized tangent bundle
          %p
            We discuss how a type II geometry is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduction+of+the+structure+group"} reduction of the structure group
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+tangent+bundle"} generalized tangent bundle
            along the inclusion
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(d) \times O(d) \to O(d,d)
          #InclusionForTypeIIGeometry.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Consider the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
              inclusion
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathrm{O}(d) \times \mathrm{O}(d)
                    \\to
                    \\mathrm{O}(d,d)
            %p
              of those
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+group"} orthogonal transformations
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bilinear+form"} bilinear form
              of signature
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mo ,
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (d,d)
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{O}(d,d)
              is presented as the group of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi d
                      %mo ×
                      %mn 2
                      %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2d \times 2d
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix"} matrices
              that preserve the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bilinear+form"} bilinear form
              given by the
              = succeed "-matrix" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi d
                      %mo ×
                      %mn 2
                      %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2d \times 2d
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo ≔
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} id
                                %mi d
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} id
                                %mi d
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\eta
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    0 &amp; \mathrm{id}_d
                    \\\
                    \\mathrm{id}_d &amp; 0
                    }
                    \\right)
            %p
              then this inclusion sends a pair
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo +
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A_+, A_-)
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+group"} orthogonal
              = succeed "-matrices" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ×
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \times n
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo +
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %msqrt
                        %mn 2
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi A
                                %mo +
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                              %msub
                                %mi A
                                %mo −
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi A
                                %mo +
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %msub
                                %mi A
                                %mo −
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi A
                                %mo +
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %msub
                                %mi A
                                %mo −
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi A
                                %mo +
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                              %msub
                                %mi A
                                %mo −
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (A_+ , A_-)
                    \\mapsto
                    \\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    A_+ + A_- &amp; A_+ - A_-
                    \\\
                    A_+ - A_- &amp; A_+ + A_-
                    }
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
          %p
            This inclusion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groups"} Lie groups
            induces the corresponding morphism of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoid"} smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stacks"} moduli stacks
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundles"} principal bundles
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi TypeII
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{TypeII}
                  \:
                  \\mathbf{B}(\mathrm{O}(d) \times \mathrm{O}(d))
                  \\to
                  \\mathbf{B} \mathrm{O}(d,d)
                  \\,.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              There is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+sequence"} fiber sequence
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoid"} smooth stacks
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo \
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi TypeII
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    O(d) \backslash O(d,d) / O(d)
                    \\to
                    \\mathbf{B}(\mathrm{O}(d) \times \mathrm{O}(d))
                    \\stackrel{\mathbf{TypeII}}{\to}
                    \\mathbf{B} \mathrm{O}(d,d)
                    \\,,
            %p
              where the fiber on the left is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset+space"} coset space
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(d) \times O(d)
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi O
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mo ,
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(d,d)
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p There is a canonical embedding
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathrm{GL}(d) \hookrightarrow \mathrm{O}(d,d)
            %p
              of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
            %p In the above matrix presentation this is given by sending
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ↦
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi a
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi a
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mi T
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    a
                    \\mapsto
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    a &amp; 0
                    \\\
                    0 &amp; a^{-T}
                    }
                    \\right)
                    \\,,
            %p
              where in the bottom right corner we have the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transpose+matrix"} transpose
              of the inverse matrix of the invertble matrix
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              Under inclusion of def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InclusionForTypeIIGeometry"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
              of a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimensional
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              defines an
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} O
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mo ,
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{O}(d,d)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊕
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mo *
                    %mi X
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                        %mi X
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    T X \oplus T^* X
                    \:
                    
                    X
                    \\stackrel{T X}{\to}
                    \\mathbf{B}\mathrm{GL}(d)
                    \\stackrel{}{\to}
                    \\mathbf{B} \mathrm{O}(d,d)
                    \\,.
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
              canonically associated to this composite cocycles may canonically be identified with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              vector bundle
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⊕
                      %msup
                        %mi T
                        %mo *
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X \oplus T^* X
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+tangent+bundle"} generalized tangent bundle
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            Therefore we may canonically consider the groupoid of
            = succeed "-twisted" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊕
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mo *
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X \oplus T^* X
            = succeed "-structures," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi TypeII
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{TypeII}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+differential+c-structures"} twisted differential c-structures
          %p
            More generally, instead of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo =
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊕
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mo *
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = T X \oplus T^* X
            one considers bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensions"} extensions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mo *
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  T^* X \to E \to T X
                  \\,.
          %p
            These may have structure froups in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(n,n)
            but not in the inclusion
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n) \hookrightarrow O(n,n)
            %em
              %a{:href => "#GeometricAndNonGeometric"} Geometric and non-geometric type II geometries
            below. Accordingly, in all of the following
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊕
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mo *
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X \oplus T^* X
            could be replaced by a more general extension
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong type II generalized vielbein
              on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mover
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mo ˜
                                %mi T
                                %mi X
                                %mo ⊕
                                %msup
                                  %mi T
                                  %mo *
                                %mi X
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi O
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ×
                            %mi O
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi T
                                  %mi X
                                  %mo ⊕
                                  %msup
                                    %mi T
                                    %mo *
                                  %mi X
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ⇙
                              %mi E
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↙
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi TypeII
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi O
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi n
                            %mo ,
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;&amp;\stackrel{\widetilde(T X \oplus T^* X)}{\to}&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}(O(n) \times O(n))
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{T X \oplus T^* X}}\searrow &amp;\swArrow_{E}&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{\mathbf{TypeII}}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B} O(n,n)
                    }
            %p
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo =
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H} =
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted cohomology
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo ∈
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi TypeII
                    %mi Struc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi O
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊕
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mo *
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi TypeII
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E
                    \\in
                    \\mathbf{TypeII}Struc(X)
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B} O(n,n)}(T X \oplus T^* X, \mathbf{TypeII})
                    \\,.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition__definition Proposition / Definition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi TypeII
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Struc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{TypeII}\mathrm{Struc}(X)
              is that of “generalized vielbein fields” on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "#GMPW"} GMPW
            %p
              In particular, its set of equivalence classes is the set of type-II generalized geometry structures on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Over a local
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+chart"} coordinate chart
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi d
                      %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^d \simeq U_i \hookrightarrow X
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} O
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mo ,
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{O}(d,d)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo =
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi e
                                %mo +
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                              %msub
                                %mi e
                                %mo −
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo +
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msubsup
                                %mi e
                                %mo +
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mi T
                              %mo −
                              %msubsup
                                %mi e
                                %mo −
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mi T
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi B
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msubsup
                                %mi e
                                %mo +
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mi T
                              %mo −
                              %msubsup
                                %mi e
                                %mo −
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mi T
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi e
                                %mo +
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %msub
                                %mi e
                                %mo −
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo −
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msubsup
                                %mi e
                                %mo +
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mi T
                              %mo +
                              %msubsup
                                %mi e
                                %mo −
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mi T
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi B
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msubsup
                                %mi e
                                %mo +
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mi T
                              %mo +
                              %msubsup
                                %mi e
                                %mo −
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mi T
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E =
                    \\frac{1}{2}
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    (e_+ + e_-) + (e_+^{-T} - e_-^{-T})B &amp; (e_+^{-T} - e_-^{-T})
                    \\\
                    (e_+ - e_-) - (e_+^{-T} + e_-^{-T})B &amp; (e_+^{-T} + e_-^{-T})
                    }
                    \\right)
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mo +
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mo −
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_+, e_- \in C^\infty(U_i, \mathrm{O}(d))
              are thought of as two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vielbein"} ordinary vielbein
              fields, and where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              is any smooth skew-symmetric
              = succeed "-matrix" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ×
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \times n
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi d
                      %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^d \simeq U_i
            %p
              By an
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} O
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} O
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{O}(d) \times \mathrm{O}(d)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformation"} gauge transformation
              this can always be brought into a form where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mo +
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mo −
                    %mo =
                    %mo :
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mn 2
                    %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_+ = e_- =: \tfrac{1}{2}e
              such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi e
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %msup
                                %mi e
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mi T
                              %mi B
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi e
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mi T
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E =
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    e &amp; 0
                    \\\
                    \- e^{-T}B  &amp; e^{-T}
                    }
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              The corresponding “generalized metric” over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mi T
                    %mi E
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi e
                                %mi T
                            %mtd
                              %mi B
                              %msup
                                %mi e
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mn 1
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi e
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mn 1
                      %mo )
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi e
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %msup
                                %mi e
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mi T
                              %mi B
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi e
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mi T
                      %mo )
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi g
                              %mo −
                              %mi B
                              %msup
                                %mi g
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mn 1
                              %mi B
                            %mtd
                              %mi B
                              %msup
                                %mi g
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mn 1
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %msup
                                %mi g
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mn 1
                              %mi B
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi g
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mn 1
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E^T
                    E
                    \=
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    e^T &amp; B e^{-1}
                    \\\
                    0  &amp; e^{-1}
